Title: Port the restored D3D9 backend to ANGLE's current D3D interfaces
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

Applied from src/ after the chromium/ series, so it can adjust what those
restore. chromium/third_party/angle/0003 through 0005 revert ANGLE's removal of
the Direct3D 9 renderer, which matters here because D3D9 is the fallback on the
old GPUs these builds target. ANGLE kept developing its shared D3D code after
deleting that backend, though, and nothing was left to notice when the shared
base classes grew requirements the D3D9 subclasses do not meet. It compiled at
Electron 44.2.0 and stopped at 44.10.2, when the ANGLE roll brought the three
changes below; Renderer9.cpp failed with "allocating an object of abstract class
type" for Image9 and every TextureStorage9 subclass.

  d3d/TextureD3D.h        restores the public hasDirtyImages() getter beside
                          resetDirty(). Both the member (mDirtyImages) and
                          resetDirty() still exist; only the getter went, since
                          upstream's remaining caller is StateManager11, which
                          resets the flag without reading it. Renderer9 reads it
                          to decide whether to force-set the texture after an
                          image update, so dropping the call instead would have
                          silently changed what gets re-bound.

  d3d9/TextureStorage9.h  TextureStorage gained four pure virtuals:
  d3d9/TextureStorage9.cpp  getLevelWidth, getLevelHeight, getLevelDepth and
                          getFormat. Implemented once on the TextureStorage9
                          base rather than on each of _2D, _Cube and _EGLImage,
                          which is possible because mTextureWidth,
                          mTextureHeight and mInternalFormat are already
                          protected members there. The width and height mirror
                          TextureStorage11's shift-and-clamp; depth is a
                          constant 1, as the D3D9 backend has no 3D textures.

  d3d9/Image9.h           ImageD3D gained pure virtual initializeContents, for
  d3d9/Image9.cpp         robust resource initialisation. Mirrors Image11: lock
                          the surface, run the format's dataInitializerFunction
                          if it has one, and otherwise zero it. The zero path is
                          the common one -- formatutils9 reads the initializer
                          out of a sparse map and most formats get nullptr --
                          and leaving it out would hand fresh textures whatever
                          was in that memory. One memset covers the locked rows,
                          which are contiguous at Pitch stride; the block-height
                          division is for the DXT formats, which store a block
                          row at a time.

Verified by building third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/d3d:angle_d3d9_backend
(143 targets, including the shared angle_d3d_shared TextureD3D.obj).

